      "content": "The trend of prioritizing political messaging in contemporary art can indeed influence its perceived value. Critics sometimes argue that this may compromise aesthetic beauty, but others appreciate the visceral impact and urgency it brings to art. Aesthetic beauty remains a subjective measure, and political art often seeks to provoke deeper thinking and emotional responses, thereby adding a different but valuable dimension to contemporary art. Ultimately, it depends on personal perspective and the criteria one uses to evaluate art's worth.",
