      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what u mean about subjectivity, but feels like a lot of modern stuff is just basically a lecture or a protest disguised as art. like, if i need to read a 5 page essay to understand why a blank canvas with a slogan is \"deep,\" hasn't the art failed? isn't the decline of actual craftsmanship and aesthetic skill a pretty objective sign that the quality of art is dropping?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
